 "final_message": "All 12 items are done, and the test suite passes (6 tests, including the two new ones).\n\n- **Items 1\u20138:** I changed `conversion_rate`, `pooled_conversion_rate`, `conversions_in_window`, `parse_session_log`, `dedupe_sessions`, `daily_conversion_counts` and `campaign_summary` to follow SPEC sections 1\u20137.\n- **Items 9\u201310:** I added a test for `None` counting as not converted, and a test that `dedupe_sessions` keeps the last duplicate id.\n- **Item 11:** In the README, `conversions_in_window` now says it sums the last `days` entries, and there is a new entry for `daily_conversion_counts`.\n- **Item 12:** Checking the rest of the package turned up three more mismatches, now fixed:\n  - `top_converting_groups` now excludes empty groups and breaks ties by group name.\n  - `conversion_rate_by_group` now maps empty groups to `None` and sorts the keys.\n  - `longest_conversion_streak` now resets the run after a day with no conversions.\n\nWhere the spec was silent, I made two choices:\n- **Unexpected `converted` value:** `parse_session_log` raises `ValueError` with the line number for any value other than `1`, `0` or empty. The spec lists no error for this case.\n- **Negative `days`:** `conversions_in_window` returns `0` for a negative `days`, the same as for `days == 0`.\n\nI didn't add tests for the other fixes, since you asked for tests on sections 1 and 5 only.",
